{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Knot.JetGradeLengthShift","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Knot.JetGradeLengthShift","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Knot.JetGradePromotion"],"declarations":17,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.JetGradeLengthShift.length_mul_sTop_ne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.JetGradeLengthShift.length_mul_sTop_ne","kind":"theorem","line":233,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/JetGradeLengthShift.lean#L233-L258","doc":"**The length always moves.** For every permutation -- no hypothesis at all --\nright multiplication by the fresh generator changes the Coxeter length. It rises\nby one when `(sub, top)` was not an inversion and falls by one when it was, so in\nparticular it is never left where it was.\n\nThis is what the Hecke relation needs: if the length could stay put, the\ndescending branch of the right-action rule would be taken twice and\n`T_s^2 = A T_s + 1` would fail. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.JetGradeLengthShift.invSet_erase_image","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.JetGradeLengthShift.invSet_erase_image","kind":"theorem","line":201,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/JetGradeLengthShift.lean#L201-L231","doc":"**Every other pair transports**, with no hypothesis on `v` at all. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.JetGradeLengthShift.mem_invSet_sub_top_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.JetGradeLengthShift.mem_invSet_sub_top_mul","kind":"theorem","line":193,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/JetGradeLengthShift.lean#L193-L199","doc":"The fresh generator flips the status of the one pair it can see. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.JetGradeLengthShift.mem_invSet_sub_top","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.JetGradeLengthShift.mem_invSet_sub_top","kind":"theorem","line":188,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/JetGradeLengthShift.lean#L188-L191","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.JetGradeLengthShift.length_mul_sTop","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.JetGradeLengthShift.length_mul_sTop","kind":"theorem","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/JetGradeLengthShift.lean#L153-L170","doc":"**The promotion theorem, as a count.** Multiplying on the right by the fresh\ngenerator raises the Coxeter length -- the Grobner-Shirshov filtration grade --\nby exactly one, for every permutation fixing the top point.\n\nThis is what `GradedGeneratingFunction.gf_shift` consumes: a degree function\nshifted by one with its coefficients untouched. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.JetGradeLengthShift.invSet_mul_sTop","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.JetGradeLengthShift.invSet_mul_sTop","kind":"theorem","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/JetGradeLengthShift.lean#L120-L151","doc":"**The inversion set moves by exactly one pair.** Everything the fresh\ngenerator can see other than `(sub, top)` is carried across by `phi`, and that\none pair is added. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.JetGradeLengthShift.phi_sub_top","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.JetGradeLengthShift.phi_sub_top","kind":"theorem","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/JetGradeLengthShift.lean#L117-L118","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.JetGradeLengthShift.phi_injective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.JetGradeLengthShift.phi_injective","kind":"theorem","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/JetGradeLengthShift.lean#L112-L115","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.JetGradeLengthShift.phi_phi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.JetGradeLengthShift.phi_phi","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/JetGradeLengthShift.lean#L109-L110","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.JetGradeLengthShift.phi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.JetGradeLengthShift.phi","kind":"def","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/JetGradeLengthShift.lean#L105-L107","doc":"Transport of ordered pairs along the fresh generator. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.JetGradeLengthShift.mem_invSet","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.JetGradeLengthShift.mem_invSet","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/JetGradeLengthShift.lean#L100-L103","doc":"Membership in the inversion set, unfolded. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.JetGradeLengthShift.sTop_lt_sTop","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.JetGradeLengthShift.sTop_lt_sTop","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/JetGradeLengthShift.lean#L71-L97","doc":"**The one-pair lemma.** For an ordered pair other than `(sub, top)`, applying\nthe fresh generator to both coordinates preserves the order. This is the fact\nthat makes the inversion count move by exactly one rather than by an unknown\namount. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.JetGradeLengthShift.sTop_apply_of_ne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.JetGradeLengthShift.sTop_apply_of_ne","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/JetGradeLengthShift.lean#L66-L69","doc":"`sTop` moves only the top two points. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.JetGradeLengthShift.le_sub_of_ne_top","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.JetGradeLengthShift.le_sub_of_ne_top","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/JetGradeLengthShift.lean#L56-L64","doc":"Everything other than the top point lies at or below `sub`, because `sub` is\nthe immediate predecessor of the maximum. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.JetGradeLengthShift.val_top","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.JetGradeLengthShift.val_top","kind":"theorem","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/JetGradeLengthShift.lean#L54-L54","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.JetGradeLengthShift.val_sub","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.JetGradeLengthShift.val_sub","kind":"theorem","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/JetGradeLengthShift.lean#L52-L52","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.JetGradeLengthShift.sTop","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.JetGradeLengthShift.sTop","kind":"def","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/JetGradeLengthShift.lean#L49-L50","doc":"The adjacent transposition of the top two points -- the \"fresh generator\". ","signatureChunk":0}]}